1
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:08,442
What happens when trading losses keep shrinking your margin balance?

2
00:00:09,182 --> 00:00:14,604
To answer that, we need to understand two levels: initial margin and maintenance margin.

3
00:00:16,504 --> 00:00:22,958
In this video, we look inside a futures account: how margin works, and what happens when equity falls.

4
00:00:25,658 --> 00:00:33,864
Margin is collateral. It is money you place in your account to support an open futures position, and to show you can meet your obligations.

5
00:00:34,204 --> 00:00:39,098
It is not a fee, it is not a down payment, and it is not the maximum you can lose.

6
00:00:41,198 --> 00:00:49,356
Initial margin is the amount required to open a position. In our example, it is RM8,000 per contract.

7
00:00:49,696 --> 00:00:58,142
Maintenance margin is the minimum equity you must keep while the position is open. In our example, RM6,000.

8
00:00:58,482 --> 00:01:06,256
These numbers are hypothetical. Actual requirements depend on clearing house requirements, market conditions and your broker's policy.

9
00:01:08,356 --> 00:01:14,498
Every trading day, open positions are marked to market. They are revalued at the day's settlement price.

10
00:01:14,838 --> 00:01:21,316
Gains are credited to your account and losses are debited. This daily cash flow is called variation margin.

11
00:01:21,656 --> 00:01:39,150
Say you are long one contract. Day one, the price falls RM40: minus RM1,000. Day two, it rises RM20: plus RM500. Day three, it falls RM80: minus RM2,000.

12
00:01:39,490 --> 00:01:48,272
In total, a loss of RM2,500. Equity falls from RM8,000 to RM5,500.

13
00:01:50,372 --> 00:01:53,322
Now look at the same account on an equity dashboard.

14
00:01:53,662 --> 00:02:02,276
RM5,500 is below the illustrative maintenance level of RM6,000. The warning line has been crossed.

15
00:02:04,376 --> 00:02:14,070
This can trigger a margin call: a request to deposit more funds, often to bring equity back up to the initial margin level, depending on your broker's terms.

16
00:02:14,410 --> 00:02:20,768
In our example, that would be RM2,500 to return to RM8,000.

17
00:02:21,108 --> 00:02:29,482
If the call is not met in time, or the market moves sharply, the broker may reduce or close your positions. This is forced liquidation.

18
00:02:29,822 --> 00:02:36,396
And remember: losses are not limited to your margin. If the account goes negative, you still owe the shortfall.

19
00:02:38,496 --> 00:02:44,734
There are two layers of margin. The clearing house sets minimum margin requirements for its clearing participants.

20
00:02:45,074 --> 00:02:52,224
Your broker may require more than that minimum from you, based on its own risk policy. What you pay is your broker's requirement.

21
00:02:54,324 --> 00:03:03,034
Margin requirements are not fixed. The clearing house reviews them, and they can be raised or lowered, especially when volatility changes.

22
00:03:03,374 --> 00:03:09,492
If margin rises, you may need more funds to hold the same position, even without making a new trade.

23
00:03:11,592 --> 00:03:14,518
Margin is collateral that supports your position.

24
00:03:14,858 --> 00:03:19,872
Initial margin opens a position; maintenance margin is the minimum to keep it.

25
00:03:20,212 --> 00:03:24,002
Positions are marked to market daily, through variation margin.

26
00:03:24,342 --> 00:03:28,924
Falling below maintenance can lead to a margin call, or forced liquidation.

27
00:03:29,264 --> 00:03:32,358
Brokers may require more than the clearing house minimum.

28
00:03:32,698 --> 00:03:36,656
Margin requirements can change, and losses can exceed margin.

29
00:03:37,956 --> 00:03:46,906
Margin is not the maximum you can lose. It is collateral to support a futures position. Managing capital is every trader's responsibility.

30
00:03:49,006 --> 00:03:52,772
This is only the foundation for understanding the futures market.

31
00:03:53,112 --> 00:03:56,110
Know the product you trade before taking any risk.

32
00:03:56,450 --> 00:03:59,520
Continue your learning with Capital Market Institute.

33
00:04:01,420 --> 00:04:07,082
The references for this video are shown on screen. Always check the latest official specifications.

34
